      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T22:21:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a discrepancy in the numbers?\n\nFrom the bug: \n\n\u003e The Official numbers for Bloonchipper list mcu power as 21.8 mW with stddev of 0.06 in idle and 0.3 mW with stddev of 0.3 in sleep. Testing is providing consistent results (on one unit!) of 16.2 mW in idle and 0.3 mW in Sleep.\n\n\nHowever, the [docs show](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/HEAD/docs/fingerprint/fingerprint.md#dragonclaw-v0_3) this:\n\n## Idle\n\n```\n@@           NAME  COUNT    AVERAGE  STDDEV        MAX        MIN\n@@   ppvar_mcu_mw   2379    16.0525  0.1395    17.1917    15.8893\n```\n\n```\n@@           NAME  COUNT    AVERAGE  STDDEV        MAX        MIN\n@@    ppvar_fp_mw   2379     0.7081  0.5254     3.1751     0.1000\n```\n\nWhen I ran the script on my bloonchipper v3, I get:\n\n```\nINFO:ppvar_fp_mw        actual: 0.73 expected: 0.60 threshold: +/-0.10\nINFO:ppvar_mcu_mw:      actual: 16.07 expected: 16.20 threshold: +/-0.10\n```\n\n## Sleep\n\n```\n@@           NAME  COUNT    AVERAGE  STDDEV        MAX        MIN\n@@    ppvar_fp_mw   2359     0.6903  0.5118     3.1751     0.1000\n```\n\n```\n@@           NAME  COUNT    AVERAGE  STDDEV        MAX        MIN\n@@   ppvar_mcu_mw   2359     0.5296  0.3512     7.0330     0.2605\n```\n\nWhen I ran the script on my bloonchipper v3, I get:\n\n```\nINFO:ppvar_fp_mw        actual: 0.81 expected: 0.60 threshold: +/-0.10\nINFO:ppvar_mcu_mw:      actual: 0.27 expected: 0.34 threshold: +/-0.13\n```\n\nIf we set the limits based on the average from the docs +/- one standard deviation, I think that will work?",
      "parentUuid": "b9f24a90_fb3114fe",
      "revId": "6e38a12b083a3dc409182b4f69c9d962bf24901c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
